<!-- ══ WHAT IS VTA ══ -->
<section class="what" id="what-is">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="what-row">
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="stag">Understanding VTA</div>
        <h2 class="stitle">Why does the<br><em>angle matter?</em></h2>
        <p class="ssub">Your stylus reads the groove at a specific angle. Getting it exactly right — for each record — is the difference between good and extraordinary sound.</p>
        <div class="what-items">
          <div class="what-item">
            <div class="what-num">VTA</div>
            <div>
              <div class="what-item-title">Vertical Tracking Angle</div>
              <p class="what-item-desc">The angle the tonearm makes with the record surface when viewed from the side. Deviations of even fractions of a millimetre affect clarity, tonal balance and soundstage.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="what-item">
            <div class="what-num">SRA</div>
            <div>
              <div class="what-item-title">Stylus Rake Angle</div>
              <p class="what-item-desc">The angle of the stylus contact relative to the groove — ideally 92°. When wrong, you'll hear harshness, reduced bass definition, and a collapsed soundstage.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="what-item">
            <div class="what-num">FLY</div>
            <div>
              <div class="what-item-title">On the Fly Adjustment</div>
              <p class="what-item-desc">Easy VTA lets you adjust while the record plays. Hear the change in real time. Finding the "sweet spot" has never been this precise or enjoyable.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal d2">
        <div class="video-wrap">
          <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/mRUqiiXkmSM" title="Easy VTA in action" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
        </div>
        <p class="video-cap">Watch Easy VTA in action — on the fly VTA adjustment while playing vinyl</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

